y\nVisit\nGive\nCollege of Engineering, Physics, and Computing\nToggle Search\nMenu\nExplore Our College\nMission & Vision\nDepartments\nCenters, Institutes, & Research\nCareer Development\nStudent Success\nFacilities & Locations\nStudent Experience & Special Programs\nExplore Our College\nPrograms & Admission\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nCertificate Programs\nPre-College Summer Program\nHow to Apply & Transfers\nScholarships & Aid\nVisit\nMore in Programs & Admission\nConnect & Contact\nLeadership & Staff\nFaculty Directory\nNews & Events\nAlumni & Giving\nContact Us\nConnect With Us\nREQUEST INFO\nAPPLY\nVISIT\nGIVE\nLet Us Help\nSearch\nSubmit Search\nHome\nFor Current Students\nGraduate Teaching and Research Assistantships\nGraduate Teaching and Research Assistantships\nIn This Section\nIn This Section\nFor Current Students\nCourse Schedules\nCourse Descriptions\nGrand Challenges Scholars Program\nCareer Resources\nFabrication Services Request - Students\nIncoming Students\nInfo for New Undergraduates\nInformation for Master's Students\nThe Current Page is Graduate TA and RA - Info & Forms\nGuidelines for PhD Studies\nPolicies for All Students\nPolicies for Graduate Students\nPolicies for Undergraduate Students\nEach department in the College of Engineering, Physics, and Computing offers Teaching Assistant (TA) and Research Assistant (RA) positions to outstanding graduate students, primarily for doctoral study.\nEach of the departments at the College of Engineering, Physics, and Computing offers teaching and research assistantships. These positions are competitive, based on academic background, GPA, research / teaching experience and potential, standard tests scores such as GRE scores and TOEFL scores. In addition, PhD students are given higher priority for consideration.\nTeaching Assistants receive a full or partial tuition scholarship and a stipend for living expenses, and assist faculty members with instruction in undergraduate and/or graduate courses.\nResearch Assistants receive a full tuition scholarship and a stipend for living expenses, and assist a faculty member on a research project, typically one that is funded by a research grant.\nFor research assistantships, we encourage prospective students to check our faculty profiles and discuss their research interests with the faculty members whose research areas match the student's interests. View faculty profiles for our College.\nTo apply for these positions, please fill out the form that corresponds to your current department or the department you have applied to.\nApplications:\nDepartment of Biomedical Engineering\nDepartment of Civil and Environmental Engineering\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartment of Electrical and Computer Engineering\nDepartment of Mechanical Engineering\nCollege of Engineering, Physics, and Computing\nPangborn Hall 334\nThe Catholic University of America\n620 Michigan Ave., NE\nWashington, DC 20064\nFacebook (Meta)\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nX (Formerly known as Twitter)\nSupport the College\nMake a gift to Catholic University\nAbout\nDepartments\nHow to Apply\nAccreditation\nContact\nResources & Support\nFor Current Students\nFor Faculty & Staff\nEmployment\nAthletics\nCardinal Shop\nLibraries\nDirectory\nCareers\nFor Media\nCopyright & Trademark\nPrivacy\nConsumer Information\nEn Espa\u00f1ol\nDisability Support\nReport Misconduct\nCompliance\nFacebook\nInstagram\nYouTube\nLinkedIn\n\u00a9 1887-2026\nThe Catholic University of America", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/current-students/graduate-teaching-and-research-assistantships#main-content"], ["", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/current-students/graduate-teaching-and-research-assistantships"], ["", "https://www.catholic.edu/"], ["Request Info", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/programs-admission/request-information"], ["Apply", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/programs-admission/how-apply-transfers"], ["Visit", "https://enginee